WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.439 --> 00:00:10.620
remember me I am the fallen soldier
sailor Airman and marine I am the one

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.949
that held the line sometimes I
volunteered

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:21.779
sometimes I went because I was told to
go but when the nation called

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:29.420
I answered in order to serve I left
behind the family friends and freedom

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:39.469
that so many take for granted over time
I used different weapons a sword a

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:46.579
musket a bayonet a rifle a machine gun

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:53.370
often I marched into battle on foot
countless miles across whole continents

00:00:53.370 --> 00:01:05.030
I had little water and even less food
but it did not matter we had a job to do

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:10.470
other times I rode to battle on
horseback or in wagons sometimes on

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:18.900
trains later in tanks or jeeps or
Humvees in early Wars my ships were made

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:26.340
of wood and powered by the wind later
they were made of steel and powered by

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:33.479
diesel fuel or the atom I even took to
the air and mastered the sky in planes

00:01:33.479 --> 00:01:43.350
helicopters and jets the machines of war
evolved and changed with the times but

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:49.079
remember that it was always me the
warrior that had to fight our nation's

00:01:49.079 --> 00:01:57.060
enemies I fought at Lexington and
Concord as our nation was born I crossed

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:06.540
the Delaware on Christmas Day in 1776
freedom was on our side I defended the

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:12.280
Chattahoochee River in the war of 1812 I
would stand again

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:19.010
in the Civil War I fought with my
brothers and against my brothers at

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:28.450
Gettysburg and Shiloh and Bull Run I
learned that we must never again divide

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:37.459
in World War one I marched on the Marne
and held the line at Bella wood the war

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:47.330
to end all wars they called it I just
called it hell in World War two

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:52.459
I fought everywhere from the beaches of
Normandy and the Battle of the Bulge to

00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:55.940
the sands of Iwo Jima and the hell of
Guadalcanal

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:05.590
I stood against tyranny and kept
darkness from consuming the world in

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:13.790
Korea I landed at Inchon and broke out
of the Chosun reservoir they called it

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:25.640
the Forgotten War but I never forgot in
Vietnam I went and I fought in the

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:34.160
Mekong Delta and an IED rang and Khe
Sanh and hamburger hill some say my

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:42.760
country wavered but I did not waver ever

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:48.950
in the recent past I fought in Grenada
Panama Somalia and other desperate

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:56.540
places around the globe and finally I
have fought in Iraq in Afghanistan in

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:07.310
Baghdad and Fallujah and Ramadi in Kunar
and Helmand and Kandahar as technology

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:12.440
advanced I use night-vision goggles and
global positioning systems and drones

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:22.150
and lasers and thermal optics but it was
still me a human being that did the work

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:26.890
it was me that patrolled up the
mom's or across the desert or through

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:32.710
the streets it was me that suffered in a
merciless heat and the bitter cold it

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:38.440
was me that went out night after night
to confront our nation's enemies and

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:46.770
confront evil face to face it was me

00:04:46.920 --> 00:05:01.890
remember me I was a warrior but also
remember that I was not only a warrior I

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:13.980
was not just a soldier sailor Airman or
marine remember also that I was a son a

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:29.380
brother a father I was a daughter a
sister a mother I was a person like you

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:39.150
a real person with hopes and dreams for
the future I wanted to have children I

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:45.340
wanted to watch my children grow up I
wanted to see my son score a touchdown

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:56.170
or shoot the winning basket I wanted to
walk my daughter down the aisle I wanted

00:05:56.170 --> 00:06:02.920
to kiss my wife again I wanted to grow
old with her and be there to hold her

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:10.510
hand when life grew hard when I told her
I would be with her until the end I

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:20.970
meant it when I told my children I would
always be there for them I meant it

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:35.940
but I gave all that away all of it on
that distant battlefield on some

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:43.349
godforsaken patch of dirt amongst the
fear and the fire and the bullets or in

00:06:43.349 --> 00:06:50.759
the sky above enemy territory filled
with fatal flak or in the unforgiving

00:06:50.759 --> 00:06:57.620
sea where we fought against the enemy
and against the depths of the abyss

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:09.030
there in those awful places I held the
line I did not waver and I did not

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:20.099
hesitate I the soldier sailor Airman or
marine I stood my ground and sacrificed

00:07:20.099 --> 00:07:36.599
my life my future my hopes my dreams I
sacrificed everything for you this

00:07:36.599 --> 00:07:47.880
Memorial Day remember me the fallen
warrior and remember me not for my sake

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:56.789
but for yours remember what I sacrificed
so you can truly appreciate the

00:07:56.789 --> 00:08:10.699
incredible treasures you have life
liberty the pursuit of happiness

00:08:10.699 --> 00:08:18.300
you have the joys of life the joys that
I gave up so that you can relish in them

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:29.370
a cool breeze in the air the gentle
spring grass on your bare feet the warm

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:43.990
Summer Sun on your face family
friends that freedom never forget where

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:55.230
it all came from it came from sacrifice
the supreme sacrifice don't waste it

00:08:55.230 --> 00:09:04.390
don't waste any of your time on this
earth live a life that honors the

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:18.520
sacrifice of our fallen heroes remember
them always and make every day Memorial

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:20.700
Day

